    "cols2_2_3_1_3": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Wed Feb 26 2020 20:37:50 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Feb 26 2020 20:37:50 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_2-3_1-3",
      "col2": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "standaloneimage_1566": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
          "description": "\r\nBeth, a Stryker volunteer, shares a tender moment with one of the children at Thi Nghe Orphanage",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Wed Feb 26 2020 20:35:58 GMT+0000",
          "srcFileRef": "/content/dam/stryker/about/news/features/vietnam-exchange/Image 7 copy.jpg",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Mar 03 2020 15:25:30 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/standaloneimage"
        }
      },
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text_666449515": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Wed Feb 26 2020 20:13:39 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p>Stryker’s work with Professor Tran began shortly after Erin Cramlet, Director, Commercial Excellence and Enablement, Medical APAC, asked how Stryker could help give back while providing employees with an enriching personal growth opportunity. Maurice Ben-Mayor, President, South Pacific, suggested that Erin contact Professor Tran for further guidance.</p>\n<p>Having a heart for his home country, Professor Tran was just starting his work in Vietnam, providing training for orthopaedic surgeons at a hospital in Ho Chi Minh City and self-funding the efforts. Occasionally, he would bring Vietnamese surgeons back to Australia for training – similar to a sabbatical. His vision was to help Vietnamese surgeons advance their capacity to deliver care within the constraints of the local healthcare environment.</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Mar 29 2021 18:26:01 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        },
        "text_666449515_copy": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Wed Feb 26 2020 20:13:39 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p>So, Erin asked, <span class=\"futura-bold\">“</span>How can Stryker help?”<br>\n</p>\n<p>At first, we provided logistical support to deliver modern training courses – an eye-opening experience for the clinical staff involved. To include non-clinical staff, the program expanded to incorporate humanitarian assistance work and the Thi Nghe Orphanage was brought on board.</p>\n<p>The Vietnam exCHANGE program was then formally launched and opened to all Stryker team members.</p>\n<p>The Thi Nghe Orphanage is a unique facility that cares for over 400 children with disabilities, many of whom are unable to walk, and the children have limited access to resources and medical care.</p>\n<p>The orphanage is a caring home to its occupants - one that Stryker employees were welcomed into with open arms. From the initial visit onward, the Stryker team has cared for the children, purchased equipment and supplies, assisted with cooking and helped the caregivers in any way possible.&nbsp;</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Mar 09 2020 19:07:33 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
    "text_copy": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Tue Mar 03 2020 16:13:26 GMT+0000",
      "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
      "text": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\"><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><br>\n <span style=\"color: #000000;\">“This experience teaches you adaptability,”</span>&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">said one Stryker volunteer.&nbsp;</span></span></span><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">“We’re not here to lead. We’re here to serve.”</span><br>\n &nbsp;</span></span></span></p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Mar 29 2021 18:11:31 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "showDimensionalBox": "true",
      "textIsRich": "true"
    },
    "cols2_1905960249": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Tue Mar 03 2020 16:29:55 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Mar 03 2020 16:29:55 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2"
    },
    "text_2072178114_copy": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Wed Feb 26 2020 20:15:05 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<p>The Vietnam exCHANGE program has evolved further over time. It has been identified that children often end up in the orphanage due to their disabilities and that early interventions, both operative and non-operative, could prevent that from happening and make significant changes to children’s lives.</p>\n<p>So today, the exCHANGE program has a greater focus on helping children sooner. The program now supports the establishment and ongoing operation of the House of Ket Noi Yeu Thuong in Ho Chi Minh City. The facility offers a supportive environment for children and their families to stay when undergoing medical assessment and intervention by the visiting orthopaedic team from Australia (under the Australian Orthopaedic Association Outreach program).</p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Mar 03 2020 16:15:57 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true"
    },
    "text_685139652_copy_": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "garrett.shue@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Wed Feb 26 2020 20:19:53 GMT+0000",
      "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
      "text": "<p>By participating in this program, we see what we can achieve when healthcare and humanity are combined.</p>\n<p>There has always been a powerful exchange of perspectives, knowledge and gratitude. And the journey so far has been extremely humbling.<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n&nbsp;</p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Mar 09 2020 19:07:57 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "backgroundColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0)",
      "textIsRich": "true"
    },
